WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.566 --> 00:00:02.909
(soft chiming music)

00:00:02.909 --> 00:00:05.478
- On a small island in
Russia stands a 300-year-old

00:00:05.478 --> 00:00:09.645
multi-domed church that was
built entirely without nails.

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:18.343
Kizhi Island is home
to two wooden churches

00:00:18.343 --> 00:00:20.516
and an octagonal bell tower that exemplify

00:00:20.516 --> 00:00:23.349
18th century Russian architecture.

00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:26.777
The largest building
on Kizhi Island is the

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:28.945
Church of the Transfiguration.

00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:32.116
One hundred and twenty feet tall and covered
in 22 domes, the church

00:00:32.116 --> 00:00:36.093
sparkles like silver when the sun hits it.

00:00:36.093 --> 00:00:38.124
It was a tradition in
Russian carpentry to build

00:00:38.124 --> 00:00:40.632
using only wooden logs
with interlocking corners

00:00:40.632 --> 00:00:44.412
and no nails or steel reinforcement.

00:00:44.412 --> 00:00:45.914
The structure was sturdy enough to survive

00:00:45.914 --> 00:00:48.223
until the 19th century when
it underwent restoration

00:00:48.223 --> 00:00:50.973
to return it to its former glory.

00:00:53.023 --> 00:00:54.623
In 1990, the island was listed as a

00:00:54.623 --> 00:00:57.503
UNESCO World Heritage site,
and today the island is

00:00:57.503 --> 00:00:59.753
a national open-air museum.

00:01:01.453 --> 00:01:03.484
It might just be a legend,
but upon completion

00:01:03.484 --> 00:01:05.842
of the structure, it was
said Kizhi's main builder

00:01:05.842 --> 00:01:08.391
cast his ax into the water and proclaimed

00:01:08.391 --> 00:01:12.558
there was not, and will not
be, another one to match it.

